  "alt": "The inference stack as layered slabs, top to bottom: serving engines (vLLM, TensorRT-LLM, SGLang); continuous batching, drawn as request lanes where a finished request frees its slot for a new one; Flash Attention, drawn as a score matrix streamed tile by tile into on-chip memory; quantization, drawn as one weight at 16, 8, and 4 bits; the paged KV cache, drawn as three sequences mapped onto scattered memory blocks; and the GPU with its memory stacks. Numbered squares, top to bottom, give the order to apply them: batching, the attention kernel, FP8 quantization, then the paged KV cache.",
  "caption": "Apply the levers in the numbered order. Continuous batching alone typically delivers 10–20× higher throughput than naive batching.",
  "embed": "<figure class=\"np-figure\">\n  <a class=\"np-figure-zoom\" href=\"/static/images/diagrams/llm-inference-optimization/inference-stack.svg\"><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 712px)\" srcset=\"/static/images/diagrams/llm-inference-optimization/inference-stack.narrow.svg\" width=\"288\" height=\"1040\"><img class=\"np-has-narrow\" src=\"/static/images/diagrams/llm-inference-optimization/inference-stack.svg\" width=\"720\" height=\"856\" alt=\"The inference stack as layered slabs, top to bottom: serving engines (vLLM, TensorRT-LLM, SGLang); continuous batching, drawn as request lanes where a finished request frees its slot for a new one; Flash Attention, drawn as a score matrix streamed tile by tile into on-chip memory; quantization, drawn as one weight at 16, 8, and 4 bits; the paged KV cache, drawn as three sequences mapped onto scattered memory blocks; and the GPU with its memory stacks. Numbered squares, top to bottom, give the order to apply them: batching, the attention kernel, FP8 quantization, then the paged KV cache.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></picture></a>\n  <figcaption>Apply the levers in the numbered order. Continuous batching alone typically delivers 10–20× higher throughput than naive batching.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
